<section class="page-intro">
  <p class="eyebrow">Work / First application</p><h1>A restaurant shift is a real test.</h1><p class="lede">The first swiftlabs.xyz application is an experimental FloCafe fork for restaurant operations. It brings a broad question into focus: can the tools a business depends on stay in that business’s hands?</p><p class="status">Experimental · No production-readiness claim</p>
</section>
<section class="editorial section">
  <h2>The direction</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Keep useful records under the owner’s control. Make access deliberate. Leave a clear path to recovery and to a different provider or maintainer.</p><p>For this experiment, staff devices are intended to use one shared restaurant service. They depend on reaching that service; independent disconnected operation and peer-to-peer replication are not established capabilities.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
  <div class="section-heading horizontal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Questions from the floor</p><h2 id="questions-title">Follow the whole shift.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="workflow-grid">
    <article>
      <span class="index">01 / Orders</span><h3>Keep the details intact.</h3><p>Can changes, modifiers and allergy notes stay clear when more than one person is working on an order?</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="index">02 / Kitchen</span><h3>Make the handoff clear.</h3><p>Does the right station receive the right information? Can staff distinguish a correction from a new order?</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="index">03 / Reconciliation</span><h3>Close with confidence.</h3><p>Can the team account for orders, adjustments and recorded tenders at the end of a shift?</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="index">04 / Recovery</span><h3>Know the way back.</h3><p>Can a business restore its records after a failure, understand what changed, and return to work?</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="evidence-panel" aria-labelledby="status-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Where things stand</p><h2 id="status-title">An experiment, with questions still open.</h2>
  <div class="evidence-grid">
    <div>
      <h3>The starting point</h3><p>FloCafe was selected following my local installation and build trial. That is a starting observation, not proof of a complete restaurant workflow.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>What still needs evidence</h3><p>The fork’s current end-to-end behavior has not been verified for this site. Device usability, shared-order integrity, recovery, peripherals and payment integrations need their own evidence before stronger claims can be made.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="evidence-footnote">Agent assistance remains a design direction. This experiment does not establish reliable autonomous operation or readiness for a live venue.</p>
</section>
